{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788300004897,"sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8b61e6db6d0bb967","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show --stat e09f063"},"output":"commit e09f063f2469975e473ebc870a012aac736e7616\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 01:36:26 2026 +0200\n\n    Enforce capital matchers and lowercase constructors for variants (gh:156)\n    \n    A variant's declared name is the matcher, capital and used only in a pattern; a value is built with the lowercase constructor. The checker now refuses a lowercase declaration (except the prelude's pub Opt/Result, tracked by gh:165), a capitalized name in value position, and a lowercase name in a pattern, each hinting the other spelling.\n    \n    The wire carries the matcher's name, so a value prints and reads as `Circle` / `\"Active\"` rather than the old lowercase data form -- the JSON-is-the-name-verbatim decision the draft already records. The corpus, its emitted-code snapshots, and the unit tests migrate to the split spelling; corpus.json regenerates.\n    \n    Human-authored: the matcher/constructor casing split (draft.md #47)\n    \n    Derived: the capital wire form (draft.md 08-28), the corpus and test migration\n    \n    Agent-invented: the string-ascription exemption, the lowercase-pattern hint, the pub-enum owner-map dedup guard\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n\n ESCALATION.md                                      |  83 ++--\n examples/shapes.toy                                |   4 +-\n site/public/corpus.json                            | 502 ++++++++++-----------\n src/check/mod.rs                                   |  94 +++-\n src/check/types.rs                                 |  52 +++\n tests/backend_jq.rs                                |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/comparison_semantics.yaml             |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/cond_branches_from_annotation.yaml    |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_input.yaml                       |   8 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs.yaml                      |  10 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs_reject.yaml               |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_match.yaml                       |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_match_default.yaml               |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_payload_variant.yaml             |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_extracted.yaml         |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_generic.yaml           |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_input.yaml             |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_jsonlines.yaml         |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_record.yaml            |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_value.yaml             |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_recursive_walk.yaml              |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input.yaml                |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input_reject.yaml         |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_payload.yaml              |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_string_ascription.yaml           |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_unit_variant.yaml                |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_variant_at_runtime.yaml          |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_vec_payload.yaml                 |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/generic_enum_input.yaml               |   6 +-\n tests/corpus/generic_enum_match.yaml               |   4 +-\n ...c_enum_of_reordered_record_crossing_a_call.yaml |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/generic_enum_payload.yaml             |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/generic_enum_two_instantiations.yaml  |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/generic_enum_unit_expectation.yaml    |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_enum_stream.yaml            |  10 +-\n tests/corpus/match_arms_from_annotation.yaml       |   6 +-\n tests/enums.rs                                     |  46 +-\n tests/generics.rs                                  |  28 +-\n tests/matcher.rs                                   |   6 +-\n tests/opt.rs                                       |   6 +-\n tests/snapshots/corpus__enum_match__jq.snap        |   4 +-\n tests/snapshots/corpus__enum_match__rust.snap      |   8 +-\n .../corpus__enum_recursive_value__js.snap          |   4 +-\n .../corpus__generic_enum_payload__go.snap          |   2 +-\n .../corpus__generic_enum_payload__rust.snap        |   6 +-\n ...nums__a_fields_pattern_on_a_scalar_payload.snap |   4 +-\n ...s__a_match_that_misses_variants_names_them.snap |   4 +-\n ..._a_pattern_naming_only_some_payload_fields.snap |   4 +-\n ..._a_unit_variant_has_nothing_to_destructure.snap |   4 +-\n ...nums__a_variant_declared_twice_in_one_enum.snap |   4 +-\n ..._input_using_the_wrong_shape_for_a_variant.snap |   4 +-\n .../matcher__a_guard_does_not_cover_a_variant.snap |   4 +-\n ...__a_scalar_enum_payload_cannot_be_a_stream.snap |   5 +-\n ...iant_is_still_refused_under_an_expectation.snap |   4 +-\n ...sing__a_capitalized_constructor_is_refused.snap |   5 +\n ...ant_casing__a_lowercase_pattern_is_refused.snap |   5 +\n ...a_lowercase_variant_declaration_is_refused.snap |   5 +\n tests/step_4.rs                                    |   2 +-\n tests/streaming.rs                                 |   8 +-\n tests/streams.rs                                   |   6 +-\n tests/type_flow.rs                                 |  26 +-\n tests/unused.rs                                    |  16 +-\n tests/variant_casing.rs                            |  43 ++\n 63 files changed, 671 insertions(+), 491 deletions(-)\n","metadata":{"output":"commit e09f063f2469975e473ebc870a012aac736e7616\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 01:36:26 2026 +0200\n\n    Enforce capital matchers and lowercase constructors for variants (gh:156)\n    \n    A variant's declared name is the matcher, capital and used only in a pattern; a value is built with the lowercase constructor. The checker now refuses a lowercase declaration (except the prelude's pub Opt/Result, tracked by gh:165), a capitalized name in value position, a