doc corpus still has 6 pages of lowercase-leading\n    variant examples plus 4 stale MISQUOTED fixtures -- a scope gap, not a\n    worker mistake.\n    \n    Split variant-checker-capital-first back to todo with a narrowed brief\n    (gate/xfail the flagged doc-corpus cases so enforcement can land now), and\n    added doc-migrate-capital-variants as a separate needs-gated follow-up for\n    the actual content migration.\n    \n    Agent-invented: the exact gating/xfail mechanism and follow-up row wording\n    (maintainer ruling specified the split, not the implementation detail)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n plans/board.yaml | 10 ++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show db0c6a2 --stat | head -40","time":{"start":1788300012347,"end":1788300012349}},"id":"prt_05efca82f001Cs7QZYD5Qcy0fy","sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","messageID":"msg_05efc94a20011rkxAD07yIJjVd"}}
