{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788300964406,"sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a0ab17a5ce3aa749","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs","newString":"/// The failures one fragment accumulates. A gated fragment (see `capital_variant_gate`) is\n/// checked for the checker's refusal instead of its stale expectation; everything else runs the\n/// outcome its fences declared.\nfn fragment_failures(f: &Fragment) -> Vec<String> {\n    if capital_variant_gate(&f.at) {\n        return gated_failures(f);\n    }\n    match &f.outcome {\n        Outcome::Output(want) => support::agreement_failures(\n            &f.at,\n            &f.program,\n            f.input.as_deref(),\n            &Expect::Output(want.clone()),\n        ),\n        Outcome::Refusal => {\n            // Compiling is checked first and separately: to `agreement_failures` a program\n            // that does not compile looks exactly like one every backend refused.\n            if let Err(e) = toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n                vec![format!(\"BROKEN  {}: does not compile: {e}\", f.at)]\n            } else {\n                support::agreement_failures(&f.at, &f.program, f.input.as_deref(), &Expect::Refusal)\n            }\n        }\n        Outcome::Error(want) => match toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n            Ok(_) => vec![format!(\n                \"COMPILED {}: claims `{want}` but the program compiles\",\n                f.at\n            )],\n            Err(e) if e.to_string() != *want => vec![format!(\n                \"MISQUOTED {}: the checker says {:?}, the page says {want:?}\",\n                f.at,\n                e.to_string()\n            )],\n            Err(_) => Vec::new(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\n/// The fragments still spelling lowercase variant names the gh:156 casing checker now refuses.","oldString":"/// The fragments still spelling lowercase variant names the gh:156 casing checker now refuses."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n@@ -146,8 +146,46 @@\n     }\n     failures\n }\n \n+/// The failures one fragment accumulates. A gated fragment (see `capital_variant_gate`) is\n+/// checked for the checker's refusal instead of its stale expectation; everything else runs the\n+/// outcome its fences declared.\n+fn fragment_failures(f: &Fragment) -> Vec<String> {\n+    if capital_variant_gate(&f.at) {\n+        return gated_failures(f);\n+    }\n+    match &f.outcome {\n+        Outcome::Output(want) => support::agreement_failures(\n+            &f.at,\n+            &f.program,\n+            f.input.as_deref(),\n+            &Expect::Output(want.clone()),\n+        ),\n+        Outcome::Refusal => {\n+            // Compiling is checked first and separately: to `agreement_failures` a program\n+            // that does not compile looks exactly like one every backend refused.\n+            if let Err(e) = toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n+                vec![format!(\"BROKEN  {}: does not compile: {e}\", f.at)]\n+            } else {\n+                support::agreement_failures(&f.at, &f.program, f.input.as_deref(), &Expect::Refusal)\n+            }\n+        }\n+        Outcome::Error(want) => match toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n+            Ok(_) => vec![format!(\n+                \"COMPILED {}: claims `{want}` but the program compiles\",\n+                f.at\n+            )],\n+            Err(e) if e.to_string() != *want => vec![format!(\n+                \"MISQUOTED {}: the checker says {:?}, the page says {want:?}\",\n+                f.at,\n+                e.to_string()\n+            )],\n+            Err(_) => Vec::new(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+\n /// The fragments still spelling lowercase variant names the gh:156 casing checker now refuses.\n /// These are gated to the checker's current refusal until the doc-migrate-capital-variants board\n /// row migrates the content and removes this list, so the checker stays enforced while `just\n /// test` goes green. The list is page:line of the opening `toylang` fence, exactly the `at` a\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-156/tests/docs.rs\n@@ -146,8 +146,46 @@\n     }\n     failures\n }\n \n+/// The failures one fragment accumulates. A gated fragment (see `capital_variant_gate`) is\n+/// checked for the checker's refusal instead of its stale expectation; everything else runs the\n+/// outcome its fences declared.\n+fn fragment_failures(f: &Fragment) -> Vec<String> {\n+    if capital_variant_gate(&f.at) {\n+        return gated_failures(f);\n+    }\n+    match &f.outcome {\n+        Outcome::Output(want) => support::agreement_failures(\n+            &f.at,\n+            &f.program,\n+            f.input.as_deref(),\n+            &Expect::Output(want.clone()),\n+        ),\n+        Outcome::Refusal => {\n+            // Compiling is checked first and separately: to `agreement_failures` a program\n+            // that does not compile looks exactly like one every backend refused.\n+            if let Err(e) = toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n+                vec![format!(\"BROKEN  {}: does not compile: {e}\", f.at)]\n+            } else {\n+                support::agreement_failures(&f.at, &f.program, f.input.as_deref(), &Expect::Refusal)\n+            }\n+        }\n+        Outcome::Error(want) => match toylang::compile(&f.program) {\n+            Ok(_) => vec![format!(\n+                \"COMPILED {}: claims `{want}` but the program compiles\",\n+                f.at\n+            )],\n+            Err(e) if e.to_string() != *want => vec![format!(\n+                \"MISQUOTED {}: the checker says {:?}, the page says {want:?}\",\n+                f.at,\n+                e.to_string()\n+            )],\n+            Err(_) => Vec::new(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+\n /// The fragments still spelling lowercase variant names the gh:156 casing checker now refuses.\n /// These are gated to the checker's current refusal until the doc-migrate-capital-variants board\n /// row migrates the content and removes this list, so the checker stays enforced while `just\n /// test` goes green. The list is page:line of the opening `toylang` fence, exactly the `at` a\n","additions":38,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/docs.rs","time":{"start":1788300964401,"end":1788300964403}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_05f0b211000101A8qoSlj6gQNf","sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","messageID":"msg_05f0b1a22001UIcPDw4UxKc7PQ"}}
