{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788301253781,"sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-abc6b88b8ea9b7df","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"docs/(guides/enums|guides/matching|reference/operators/comparison|reference/types/enum|tutorial/04-enums|tutorial/06-matching).md:[0-9]+\" LAND-FAILURE.txt | sed -E 's/.*BROKEN[[:space:]]+([^:]+:[0-9]+):.*/\\1/' | sort -u"},"output":"29:    MISQUOTED docs/reference/types/enum.md:34: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `point` of `Shape` as `Point`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `point` (at byte 13)\", the page says \"a match over `Shape` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `point` (at byte 73)\"\n30:    MISQUOTED docs/reference/types/enum.md:67: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `arr` of `Json` as `Arr`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `arr` (at byte 12)\", the page says \"type `Json` is written in terms of itself (at byte 49)\"\n52:    MISQUOTED docs/tutorial/06-matching.md:67: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `a` of `S` as `A`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `a` (at byte 9)\", the page says \"a match over `S` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `b` (at byte 23)\"\n7:    MISQUOTED docs/guides/matching.md:54: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `a` of `S` as `A`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `a` (at byte 9)\", the page says \"a match over `S` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `b` (at byte 23)\"\ndocs/guides/enums.md:13\ndocs/guides/matching.md:66\ndocs/reference/operators/comparison.md:28\ndocs/reference/types/enum.md:7\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:20\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:40\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:6\n","metadata":{"output":"29:    MISQUOTED docs/reference/types/enum.md:34: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `point` of `Shape` as `Point`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `point` (at byte 13)\", the page says \"a match over `Shape` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `point` (at byte 73)\"\n30:    MISQUOTED docs/reference/types/enum.md:67: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `arr` of `Json` as `Arr`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `arr` (at byte 12)\", the page says \"type `Json` is written in terms of itself (at byte 49)\"\n52:    MISQUOTED docs/tutorial/06-matching.md:67: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `a` of `S` as `A`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `a` (at byte 9)\", the page says \"a match over `S` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `b` (at byte 23)\"\n7:    MISQUOTED docs/guides/matching.md:54: the checker says \"a variant name starts with a capital letter; declare `a` of `S` as `A`, and build its value with the lowercase constructor `a` (at byte 9)\", the page says \"a match over `S` must cover every variant or end in a default; missing `b` (at byte 23)\"\ndocs/guides/enums.md:13\ndocs/guides/matching.md:66\ndocs/reference/operators/comparison.md:28\ndocs/reference/types/enum.md:7\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:20\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:40\ndocs/tutorial/04-enums.md:6\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"docs/(guides/enums|guides/matching|reference/operators/comparison|reference/types/enum|tutorial/04-enums|tutorial/06-matching).md:[0-9]+\" LAND-FAILURE.txt | sed -E 's/.*BROKEN[[:space:]]+([^:]+:[0-9]+):.*/\\1/' | sort -u","time":{"start":1788301253776,"end":1788301253780}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The diff looks clean and coherent. Let me double check one thing: the module docstring says \"six pages still spell variant names lowercase\". Let me verify the count: the flagged fragments span these files:\n- docs/guides/enums.md\n- docs/guides/matching.md\n- docs/reference/operators/comparison.md\n- docs/reference/types/enum.md\n- docs/tutorial/04-enums.md\n- docs/tutorial/06-matching.md\n\nThat's 6 distinct files. Good.\n\nNow, the brief mentions an important detail: \"leave a comment at the gate pointing to that row\" (doc-migrate-capital-variants). My docstrings reference \"doc-migrate-capital-variants\" in:\n1. Module docstring (lines 20-22 area).\n2. `capital_variant_gate` docstring.\n3. `gated_failures` docstring + the GATED error message.\n\nThat's covered. Good.\n\nNow about provenance and the commit message per AGENTS.md:\n- The commit message subject: what changed.\n- Body: why, or what was ruled out, plus provenance lines.\n- Provenance: what's the provenance of my change?\n  - The gate mechanism itself: the brief said \"gate or xfail exactly the flagged cases ... leave a comment at the gate pointing to that row.\" The exact mechanism (list of page:line + assert-still-refused-for-casing) is my implementation choice. Per the reshape commit db0c6a2: \"Agent-invented: the exact gating/xfail mechanism and follow-up row wording (maintainer ruling specified the split, not the implementation detail)\". So my mechanism is agent-invented (there was more than one reasonable option: pure skip vs assert-still-refused; extraction vs inline).\n  - The flagged case list: derived from LAND-FAILURE.txt / the board row (the brief quoted the paths/lines verbatim as given).\n  - The extraction of fragment_failures: derived (a forced consequence of keeping the gate clean / a style consequence). Actually the extraction was my choice to avoid complexity regression — that's agent-invented too (a real decision: extract vs inline-guard vs Gated variant).\n\nPer AGENTS.md commit format:\n```\n<subject>\n\n<why / what ruled out>\nHuman-authored: ...\nDerived: ...\nAgent-invented: ...\n\nCo-Authored-By: <agent identifier>\n```\n\nMy provenance lines:\n- Derived: the flagged fragment list (from LAND-FAILURE.txt / board row variant-checker-capital-first).\n- Agent-invented: the gate mechanism (assert still-refused-for-casing rather than a silent skip), the page:line list as the gate key, and the fragment_failures extraction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: I'm \"DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode\" per the brief: \"work committed on this branch per AGENTS.md with the provenance line 'Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.'\"\n\nHmm, the brief says add the provenance line \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" and AGENTS.md says agents must add a `Co-Authored-By` trailer. Let me look at how prior commits on this branch did it. From e09f063's message: it had \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" as the last line (no Co-Authored-By trailer). Let me check the reshape commit db0c6a2: \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\". So both conventions appear. The brief explicitly says \"with the provenance line 'Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.'\" — I'll use that as the trailer, matching the prior DeepSeek commit (e09f063) on this branch. Actually, to satisfy both AGENTS.md's Co-Authored-By requirement and the brief, let me check e09f063's exact format again:\n\nFrom the `git show --stat e09f063` output earlier, the message ended with:\n```\n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n```\nNo Co-Authored-By line. Since the brief explicitly specifies the provenance line format, I'll follow it exactly: \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\"\n\nWait, but AGENTS.md says \"Agents may commit in this repository, and must add the `Co-Authored-By` trailer when they do.\" Hmm. There's a tension: AGENTS.md wants a Co-Authored-By trailer; the brief wants \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" as the provenance line. The brief is the more specific instruction for THIS lane and matches the prior DeepSeek commit style on this branch. Let me include both? Or follow the prior DeepSeek commit exactly?\n\nLet me look at how other commits by DeepSeek/this lane formatted. Let me check a couple of commits authored around this branch. Actually e09f063 (the checker commit, also \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\") is the direct precedent on this exact lane. I'll match it exactly: end the message with \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\"\n\nHmm, but to be safe with AGENTS.md, let me include a Co-Authored-By trailer too. AGENTS.md says \"must add the Co-Authored-By trailer\". The brief says \"with the provenance line 'Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.'\". \n\nLooking at db0c6a2 (the Claude commit): \n```\nAgent-invented: the exact gating/xfail mechanism and follow-up row wording (maintainer ruling specified the split, not the implementation detail)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\nSo that commit used Co-Authored-By, no \"Written by\" line.\n\ne09f063 (DeepSeek):\n```\nAgent-invented: the string-ascription exemption, the lowercase-pattern hint, the pub-enum owner-map dedup guard\n\nWritten by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n```\nSo DeepSeek used \"Written by\", no Co-Authored-By.\n\nThe brief for THIS lane explicitly says the provenance line is \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" So I'll match e09f063: use \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" as the closing line. This is the lane's established convention and the brief's explicit instruction.\n\nNow the commit message. Let me draft:\n\nSubject: \"Gate the doc-corpus fragments the capital-variant checker now refuses\"\n\nBody: why/what ruled out + provenance.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\nGate the doc-corpus fragments the variant-casing checker now refuses\n\nThe gh:156 casing enforcement (e09f063) is correct, but six docs pages still\nspell variant names lowercase, so every_fragment_is_a_real_program failed `just\ntest`: 7 BROKEN fragments the checker refuses plus 4 MISQUOTED fixtures whose\nerror fences name a later error the casing rule now shadows. Gated here instead\nof migrating, per the issue-156 reshape ruling -- the doc-migrate-capital-variants\nboard row owns the content migration and removes this gate. The gate is not a\nskip: a gated fragment must still be refused for the casing rule, so it trips if\na fragment starts compiling or fails for any other reason. The per-fragment\noutcome dispatch moves into fragment_failures so the gate lands without growing\nthe harness's cognitive complexity.\n\nDerived: the flagged page:line list (LAND-FAILURE.txt / the board row)\nAgent-invented: the gate mechanism (assert still-refused-for-casing instead of a silent skip, keyed by page:line, tripping on any other outcome), and the fragment_failures extraction\n\nWritten by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n```\n\nHmm, that's a bit long but reasonable. Let me tighten it per AGENTS.md style (concise, no bullets duplicating the diff).\n\nLet me reconsider the subject line. The repo uses imperative subjects. \"Gate the doc-corpus fragments the variant-casing checker now refuses\" — decent.\n\nLet me also reconsider whether the provenance categories are right:\n- The flagged list (11 page:line entries) — these came from LAND-FAILURE.txt (land-gate output) and the board row variant-checker-capital-first, which the brief quoted verbatim. That's \"derived\" (follows from constraints already present).\n- The gate mechanism — agent-invented (brief left the exact mechanism to me; prior reshape commit db0c6a2 already classified the mechanism as agent-invented).\n- The fragment_failures extraction — this is a style/code-shape decision (agent-invented, a real decision with alternatives).\n\nLet me finalize. First let me confirm the \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\" line — brief says: `work committed on this branch per AGENTS.md with the provenance line \"Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\"`\n\nSo my commit message will include that exact line at the end.\n\nLet me stage only tests/docs.rs (NOT LAND-FAILURE.txt — it's a scratch/untracked file I should not commit; the brief says scratch files I can't delete are fine, just don't git add them).\n\nLet me create the commit. Per the brief and AGENTS.md, agents may commit in this repo. I'll use git add + git commit.\n\nThe commit message with the multi-line body — I need to pass it to git commit. Multi-line messages via `git commit -m` are fine (multiple -m flags or a heredoc). But heredocs are denied. I can use multiple `-m` flags:\n- `git commit -m \"subject\" -m \"body paragraph\" ...`\n\nActually git commit -m \"...\" with embedded newlines in the quoted string is fine too (quoted multi-line in a single -m). Let me use multiple -m flags for clarity, or a single -m with newlines in the quotes. The instructions say multi-command bash lines are denied — I'll run `git add` and `git commit` as separate calls (they must be sequential anyway).\n\nLet me stage first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05f0f951e001AEtdjnjFDsPrI4","sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","messageID":"msg_05f0ea22f001bNDYSWmMnfHQoY"}}
