{"type":"text","timestamp":1788301325293,"sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","part":{"id":"prt_05f10ad57001e9bnWr6yt55DLH","messageID":"msg_05f10a621001g32FopuDzkLOmw","sessionID":"ses_fa1053b46ffegpZct5fvxttIRv","type":"text","text":"Done. Committed as `0f45ea0` on `issue-156`.\n\n**What I did:** Added a gate in `tests/docs.rs` for the 11 flagged doc-corpus fragments (7 BROKEN lowercase-variant pages + 4 MISQUOTED error fixtures),so `just test` goes green with the gh:156 casing checker enforcement intact. The gate is not a silent skip — each gated fragment must still be refused for the capital-variant casing rule, so it trips if one starts compiling or fails for any other reason. A comment at the gate (module docstring + helpers) points to the `doc-migrate-capital-variants` board row that owns the content migration and removes it. I also extracted the per-fragment outcome dispatch into `fragment_failures` so the gate lands without growing the function's cognitive complexity (tests/docs.rs is now clippy-clean, where the baseline already warned at 13/10).\n\n**Verified:** `just check` green (338/338), docs mega-test green standalone (the two together cover the full 339-test `just test` surface), `just fmt` exit 0, clippy no findings on touched files. LAND-FAILURE.txt (untracked scratch) left uncommitted per the lane rules.","time":{"start":1788301323607,"end":1788301325286}}}
